    {
      "id": 262329,
      "name": "MindWanderer",
      "username": "MindWanderer",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
      "created_at": "2025-02-05T19:56:18.047Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group quote-modified\" data-username=\"Sea-Envy\" data-post=\"4\" data-topic=\"31319\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/sea-envy/48/1849_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Sea-Envy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>They forgot that they already told the Ambuscade vs werewolf Haka story.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I laughed so hard at that.  I understand them forgetting some lore they dropped here and there, but forgetting a whole episode is a new one.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"TakeWalker\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"31319\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/48/5677_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TakeWalker:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>How have I never heard anyone refer to close-quarters combat as CQC before? That sounds so much cooler!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>You have not played a Metal Gear Solid game, then. That’s the only other place I’ve ever heard it, but it’s used extensively.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"TakeWalker\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"31319\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/48/5677_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TakeWalker:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Who came up with Virtuoso of the Void Jim Brooks? What a concept!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>If he’s the Golden Gunman, he shouldn’t be a Virtuoso. But now I really want to come up with whole lines of alternate Void adepts. The Veterans of the Void, the Voyagers of the Void, etc.</p>",
